--TEST--
`covariant` is written only on a property that narrows the topmost declaration's type, with a type `is` tests in constant time, that keeps its qualifier and fits its parent's narrowed type, and a property narrower than the topmost declaration's without it names `covariant` in its help — `rule:classes/a-covariant-type-is-checked-where-a-value-enters`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}
class Cat extends Animal {}

class Home {
    public Animal $pet;
    public array<mixed> $list = [];
    public tainted string $name = "";
    public function constructor() { $this->pet = new Dog(); }
}

class SameHome extends Home {
    public covariant Animal $pet;
}

class ListHome extends Home {
    public covariant array<int> $list = [];
}

class CleanHome extends Home {
    public covariant string $name = "";
}

class PlainDogHome extends Home {
    public Dog $pet;
}

class DogHome extends Home {
    public covariant Dog $pet;
}

class CatHome extends DogHome {
    public covariant Cat $pet;
}

class RepeatHome extends DogHome {
    public Dog $pet;
}

class Stray {
    public covariant Dog $pet;
    public function constructor() { $this->pet = new Dog(); }
}
// covers: lang:classes/covariant
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0882]: `covariant` has no effect here, because `$pet` is not narrower than in `Home`
%A
error[E0883]: a `covariant` property cannot have the type `array<int>`
%A
error[E0866]: `CleanHome::$name` is `string`, and `Home::$name` is `tainted string`. `covariant` keeps the `tainted` qualifier
%A
error[E0866]: `PlainDogHome::$pet` is `Dog`, and `Home::$pet` is `Animal`
%A
   = help: both classes use the same property, and `Home` writes it as `Animal`. To take a narrower type, write `covariant` before it. Each value is then tested when it is written
%A
error[E0866]: `CatHome::$pet` is `Cat`, which is not narrower than `Dog` in `DogHome`
%A
error[E0866]: `RepeatHome::$pet` is `Dog`, and `Home::$pet` is `Animal`
%A
error[E0882]: `covariant` has no effect here, because no parent class of `Stray` declares `$pet`
%A
error: aborting due to 7 errors
